OL,3,AFight over fossil fuels leaves COP31
OL,4,Aclimate talks in deadlock
OL,5,
OL,6,FNegotiations at the COP31 UN climate
OL,7,Fsummit in Turkey are in deadlock after
OL,8,Frunning more than 36 hours into
OL,9,Fovertime with countries unable to agree
OL,10,Fon a new global climate deal.
OL,12,FThe EU and Pacific island nations are
OL,13,Famongst a group pushing back against
OL,14,Fthe latest draft agreement which
OL,15,Fincluded no reference to reducing the
OL,16,Fworld's demand for fossil fuels.
OL,18,FA second sticking point involves a push
OL,19,Ffrom the Africa Group to get
OL,20,Fcommitments on more money for
OL,21,Fadaptation - but the EU has previously
OL,22,Fsaid it would not support this.
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG10/38
